sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/run/biomineral-form-physical-vs-biological-control--grok-4-7--2--2026-11-01> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Run of approach biomineral-form-physical-vs-biological-control--grok-4-7--2 (2026-11-01): completed, settled its target" ;
    dct:description "Lean 4 (ThompsonLaws.TwelvePentagons), no sorry, standard axioms only. From Euler's formula and trivalent vertex and face handshaking, a spherical lattice of pentagons and hexagons has exactly twelve pentagons, and a second theorem shows the count is independent of an arbitrary material parameter. This completes the proposed mathematical approach: one topological integer is material-independent. It does not prove 120-degree angles, regularity, vesicle templating or that radiolarian shells satisfy the hypotheses, so the three related claims are recorded as not formalized rather than given a stub proof." ;

    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/biomineral-form-physical-vs-biological-control> ;
